    "title": "Where to watch North Carolina vs VCU in March Madness First Round: Time, TV Channel",
    "text": "Updated March 19, 2026, 11:57 a.m. ETMarch Madness is underway and college basketball's big dance continues with No. 6 seed North Carolina taking on No. 11 seed VCU in a First Round matchup on Thursday, March 19. Here's everything you need to know to tune in for the clash between the Rams and Tar Heels.USA TODAY Sports has a team of journalists covering men's March Madness to keep you up to date with every point scored, rebound grabbed and game won in the 68-team tournament.Join the USA TODAY Bracket Challenge to win $1 millionWhat time is VCU vs North Carolina First Round game?No. 6 North Carolina vs No. 11 VCU tips off at 6:50 PM (EST) on Thursday, March 19 from Bon Secours Wellness Arena (Greenville, South Carolina).What channel is VCU vs North Carolina First Round game?No. 6 North Carolina vs No. 11 VCU is airing live on TNT (watch live with Sling).How to stream VCU vs North Carolina First Round gameNo. 6 North Carolina vs No. 11 VCU is available to stream on Sling.Watch the NCAA Tournament all March long with SlingMen's March Madness schedule todaySee the schedule, live scores and results for all of Thursday's NCAA Tournament action here.2026 March Madness datesMarch 17-18: First FourMarch 19-20: First RoundMarch 21-22: Second RoundMarch 26-27: Sweet 16March 28-29: Elite 8April 4: Final FourApril 6: National ChampionshipWatch UNC vs. VCU with SlingOur team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.Information in this article was imported automatically into a template written and reviewed by a USA TODAY Sports editor. You can send feedback using this form.",
